Going back through our own mail on Millbrook turned up something that does =
not<br />
help us.<br />
<br />
September 22 2020, Brill to Quarterman: discharge temp on B-3 running about=
 thirty<br />
degrees over, the valve is on its way out, it needs to be scheduled before =
it takes<br />
the compressor with it. Field note attached to that message, and it is the =
only<br />
place it exists - the 2023 migration did not carry pre-2022 technician note=
s,<br />
which is why the export does not have it.<br />
<br />
Quarterman's reply the same evening: put it in the notes on 109331 and we w=
ill pick<br />
it up when they open something on B-3.<br />
<br />
So we knew in September 2020, we wrote it down, and we parked it pending a =
customer<br />
order that was not opened for nearly eight months. That is eleven months be=
fore the<br />
rack failed in exactly the way Brill said it would.
